---
/** /free-classic-movies: every public domain film we play, plus how we check them. */

interface Card { slug: string; name: string; year: string; image: string; genres: string[]; runtimeMinutes: number }
interface Props { films: Card[]; coming: { slug: string; name: string; year: string; freeOn: string }[] }
const { films, coming } = Astro.props;
const year = new Date().getUTCFullYear();
---
<div class="wrap">
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1>Free Classic Movies</h1>
    <p class="lede">Full-length classic films you can watch free and legally, because they're in the public domain in the United States. Every one is checked before it goes up, and re-checked every week.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="grid grid--cards">
    {films.map((m) => (
      <a class="movie-card" href={`/movies/${m.slug}`}>
        <span class="frame"><img src={m.image} alt="" width="480" height="270" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></span>
        <h2 class="movie-card__title">{m.name}</h2>
        <span class="movie-card__year">{m.year} · {m.genres[0]} · {m.runtimeMinutes} min</span>
      </a>
    ))}
  </div>

  {coming.length > 0 && (
    <section class="band" aria-labelledby="coming">
      <h2 id="coming">Coming soon</h2>
      <p>Every 1 January, another year of films enters the US public domain. These play here in full from the day they're free:</p>
      <ul>{coming.map((c) => <li><a href={`/movies/${c.slug}`}><strong>{c.name}</strong> ({c.year})</a>: free in the US from {c.freeOn}</li>)}</ul>
    </section>
  )}

  <section class="band prose" aria-labelledby="how">
    <h2 id="how">How we make sure every film is free to show</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Old enough, or properly lapsed.</strong> Films first published in the US {year - 96} or earlier are out of copyright by age (95-year term). Newer films only qualify if they are American and their copyright lapsed for a missing notice or renewal, and we cite where that's recorded.</li>
      <li><strong>The story has to be free too.</strong> If a film is based on a book, play or song that someone still owns, we don't show it, even if the film itself lapsed.</li>
      <li><strong>The plain original only.</strong> No restored, colourised, re-scored or narrated versions: those can carry new copyright of their own.</li>
      <li><strong>US visitors only.</strong> Public domain rules differ by country, so the player only starts in the United States.</li>
      <li><strong>Checked every week</strong> against Wikidata, Wikipedia's list of US public domain films and the Internet Archive copy we play.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="free-film__small">Rights enquiries: <a href="mailto:hello@movietrailer.channel?subject=Rights%20enquiry">hello@movietrailer.channel</a>.</p>
  </section>
</div>
